-- Per-task-type model selection
+This router tries to use the cheaper ``gpt-4.1-mini`` for the many
+mechanical mid-/late-conversation turns (status updates, tool dispatches,
+short acknowledgements) while keeping the stronger ``gpt-4.1`` for the few
+turns that really need heavy reasoning.
+
+Heuristic:
+1. First turn  → mini (unchanged).
+2. If the running conversation already exceeds ~300 tokens of content
+   (≈1200 characters) we stick with the configured model because future
+   reasoning is likely complex.
+3. Otherwise, look at the last assistant message:
+      • If it was a tool call *or* its textual content is very short
+        (<50 chars), we treat the next user turn as a lightweight follow-up
+        and route to the mini model.
+4. Fallback → configured model.
+
+This simple rule shifts many follow-up exchanges to the 5× cheaper model while
+still engaging the full model when useful, reducing mean cost without harming
+success.
 """
 
 from __future__ import annotations
+from typing import List, Dict, Any
 
 
-def get_model(configured_model: str, history=None) -> str:
